    "open_questions": [
      "This is Duran Duran's Roger Andrew Taylor (born 1960), not Queen's Roger Meddows Taylor (drummer:roger-taylor).",
      "His kit in 1980-85: Live Aid shows a white Tama kit and a rack of long black tube toms (Octobans, as he says he used on the Power Station record); the Songsterr tabs name a Tama Imperialstar without a source; no period interview on gear was found.",
      "How much of the early records is a drum machine under him: Hungry Like the Wolf keeps a TR-808; Save a Prayer and Planet Earth have sequencers; Is There Something I Should Know? had his drums replaced with triggered samples. Which other tracks are layered is not documented here.",
      "The Westword interview refused the fetch; its Tony Thompson passage is cited from the search excerpt. Period interviews (Smash Hits, International Musician, 1981-85) were not found."
    ]
  },
