    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "composer"],
    "summary": "Duran Duran's drummer from 1979 to 1985 and again from 2001: a Birmingham drummer who taught himself by playing to records, and who with John Taylor put Chic's rhythm section under a new-wave band. Tony Thompson was 'a very big influence'. On the early records the kick is on every beat (Planet Earth, Hungry Like the Wolf) or pushes round it (Girls on Film), the hat runs in sixteenths with one hand (Rio, The Reflex), the snare sits on 2 and 4 with few fills. He left after Live Aid in 1985, exhausted; Steve Ferrone played on Notorious. Since 2001 a hybrid kit, the Tama beside a V-Drum kit and triggered samples."
  },
